      "math_academy_id": "q-109961",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=28$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=23.$ Find $\\text{Var}[5X-2Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[5X-2Y]={(5)}^{2}\\cdot 28+{(-2)}^{2}\\cdot 23=792.\n$$",
